# CSS Best Practices - STRICTLY ENFORCE

## CSS Modules Architecture - MANDATORY
- Import styles as `import styles from './Component.module.css'`
- Use camelCase naming for CSS Module classes: `.headerRow1`, `.componentCard`, `.sectionTitle`
- Each component must have its own .module.css file in the same directory

## File Structure Requirements
```
src/components/ComponentName/
  ├── ComponentName.jsx
  └── ComponentName.module.css
```

## CSS Module Class Usage
```javascript
// CORRECT
import styles from './Component.module.css';
<div className={styles.container}>
<h1 className={styles.title}>

// INCORRECT - global classes
<div className="container">
<h1 className="title">
```

## Global CSS Restrictions
- globals.css: ONLY CSS resets, typography, and CSS custom properties
- variables.css: ONLY :root custom properties
- NO component-specific styles in global files
- NO utility classes (use CSS Modules instead)

## CSS Custom Properties Pattern
```css
/* globals.css */
:root {
  --color-primary: #1a4d5c;
  --spacing-md: 1rem;
  --border-radius: 8px;
}

/* Component.module.css */
.card {
  background: var(--color-primary);
  padding: var(--spacing-md);
  border-radius: var(--border-radius);
}
```

## CSS Best Practices Rules
- NEVER use `!important` declarations - refactor specificity instead
- Use CSS custom properties (--variables) for reusable values
- Prefer flexbox and grid over floats and positioning
- Use relative units (rem, em, %) over fixed pixels when appropriate
- Follow BEM-like naming within modules: `.card`, `.cardTitle`, `.cardContent`

## Responsive Design Rules
- Use mobile-first media queries
- Standard breakpoints: 480px (mobile), 768px (tablet), 1024px (desktop), 1200px (large)
- Container max-width: 1200px with auto margins for centering
- Full-width sections with centered content containers

## CSS Property Order
1. Display & positioning
2. Box model (width, height, padding, margin)
3. Typography
4. Visual (background, border, shadow)
5. Animations & transitions

## Forbidden Patterns
- ❌ `!important` declarations
- ❌ Global CSS classes for components
- ❌ Inline styles (except dynamic values)
- ❌ Deep selector nesting (max 2 levels)
- ❌ Fixed z-index values (use CSS custom properties)
- ❌ Magic numbers (use named variables)

## Required Patterns
- ✅ CSS Modules for all component styles
- ✅ CSS custom properties for reusable values
- ✅ Semantic class names
- ✅ Mobile-first responsive design
- ✅ Consistent spacing scale
- ✅ Proper accessibility (focus states, contrast)

## Component CSS Template
```css
/* Component.module.css */
.component {
  /* Use CSS custom properties */
  background: var(--color-background);
  padding: var(--spacing-lg);
  
  /* Responsive */
  display: grid;
  gap: var(--spacing-md);
}

.component:hover {
  /* Smooth transitions */
  transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  transform: translateY(-2px);
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .component {
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
  }
}
```

## Error Prevention
- Lint CSS Module imports to ensure they exist
- Check for unused CSS classes in modules
- Validate that all colors use CSS custom properties
- Ensure no global classes are used in JSX className attributes
- Verify responsive design at specified breakpoints
